swashbuckling on the seven seas can lead  to a whole lot of danger the pirates of  the caribbean cast and crew grew to know  this well over the years seeing brutal  injuries and very close calls on set  let's check out 15 of the injuries this  cast and crew suffered while on set  number one  this doesn't sound fun filming the  pirates of the caribbean films over the  years has been hard on death's body  filming on stranger tides depp explained  that he had a bit of a physical ailment  i must have done something to my back  during a stunt and ended up with this  bad sciatic situation and how was he  feeling exactly well the actor described  it as horrible grinding electricity  unfortunately with so much money on the  line and a tight filming schedule the  actor couldn't stop and take time off to  recover he had no choice but to film  through the pain while he looked great  on screen depp was limping around the  set when the cameras weren't rolling  number two a first aid kit was always  close by caia scotlario made her mark as  a newcomer in the pirates franchise and  threw herself into the deep end  unfortunately she did wind up suffering  a bit of damage filming dead men telno  tales saw the actress fall on set  leaving her with an arm injury so bad  she was stuck in a sling for a while it  costs to be a pirate with this crew  number three this one lasted for a while  it was only the second film when johnny  depp was injured so badly on set that he  literally suffered nerve damage in his  left foot filming the big wheel scene  that featured captain jack swashbuckling  on top of the wheel while it was rolling  along was dangerous to film no doubt but  what's ironic is that it was one of the  safety measures in place that did the  most damage depp was strapped onto the  wheel tight to make sure he wouldn't  fall off but because they filmed for  such a long time the injury was  unexpectedly rough deck was pretty  honest about how serious it got  explaining i had no feeling you could  stick a pin in it and i wouldn't have  felt it note to self don't pull any  straps too tight ever again  number four she's expected to sword  fight in a corset kira knightley's first  foray into the pirates world saw her  wearing a very very tight corset while  filming including for throughout her  more stunt heavy and physically  demanding scenes to say she was  uncomfortable is an understatement  because when you got a corset on my  waist was about 20 inches and you  absolutely can't breathe fortunately  following the first film nightly was  dressed in more practical clothing for  the action she was tackling  number five you've heard of a flying  dutchman but flying wood it's not really  something you want to know about  unfortunately johnny depp came face to  face with flying wood and he can attest  that it's a brutal experience not all of  the ropes between the ships were cut  once the interceptor started to move and  the boats came apart a bit the ropes  between the ships came ripping down  catching everyone in the production off  guard to make matters worse the lions  were knocking large beams of wood on the  ship out of place leaving one flying  directly into johnny depp the actor was  hit in the right knee so badly he was  knocked out of the frame completely you  know he was limping for a while after  that one  number six it looked and felt pretty  rough by the time filming had wrapped  for stellen skarsgard on the pirate set  he was looking more and more like his  character without the prosthetics on the  bootstrap bill turner actor was fully  made up to look like his character which  meant there were a painful 4 hours spent  in the makeup chair before even starting  work when the filming did begin it was a  race against time because the makeup and  prosthetics started to really aggravate  the actor's skin skarsgard's face was  getting covered in rashes forcing the  production to limit themselves to  filming with the actor for only three  days at a time just to allow his skin  the chance to breathe and recover hoping  to prevent any permanent damage if that  weren't bad enough a full hour and a  half was spent at the end of the day  removing it all  number seven it's a risky business  johnny depp's stunt double tony  angelotti saw what was essentially the  end of his career while filming dead  man's chest the yo-yo stunt that sees  one captain jack sparrow spinning out of  control went tragically wrong and  angelotti really did spin out of control  doing a rehearsal only to be left  hanging by his leg after an 80 foot drop  what went wrong the stuntman explained  when i was up looking down i gave the  call of three two one go they pulled my  quick release that would allow me to  unravel however the operator of the  descender did not have the brake on and  i went into a free fall the performer  was in seriously rough shape suffering a  bad acl injury that needed  reconstructive surgery and severe  internal bleeding resulting in a total  loss of six units of blood and going  through it was just as painful as it  sounds angelotti described it saying i  spun so uncontrollably fast that the  centrifugal force actually ripped my  pelvis apart i felt the ripping inside  my pelvic area the burning ripping  sensation after a long time spent in a  wheelchair learning how to walk again  the stuntman returned to sets doing some  lighter stunt work and stunt  coordinating work but his career would  never be the same as it was before that  accident  number eight yes seriously this beard  was literally on fire throwing back to  curse of the black pearl we've got  jacoby played by vince lozano who wound  up being a risk to himself and others on  set because of his literal flaming beard  instead of resorting to cg the special  effects and makeup team went all out  making a full fake beard with wires  hidden inside that would allow for  incense to be lit releasing smoke while  filming any time the smoke would let up  the beard would get relit once again  however sometimes it got a bit out of  control and the beard fully caught fire  you kind of always smell burning hair  around this guy both the actor and  people around him were left with some  nasty burns from the long beard hair  whipping around  number 9. swords equal danger pretty  much all of the time before his near  fatal injury tony angelotti suffered a  sword to the face while battling orlando  bloom it was time to film their  blacksmith forge fight but things  started to go haywire when as angelotti  put it orlando i think got lost at one  point and went in another direction and  i ducked back and the tip of its blade  caught right near my eyebrow it was a  very close call and while the stunt  director was ready to move on johnny  depp was quick to insist angelotti get  the right treatment and be checked over  by a medic fortunately angelotti only  suffered a small scar in the end of that  one  number 10 putting things in your eyes  often leads to some struggle keira  knightley was wearing colored contact  lenses in the first pirates of the  caribbean movie these lenses were  outfitted so she had dark spots in the  center with a lighter color around them  the problem with these lenses though was  that they made the actress extremely  dizzy and unable to do her job nightly  knew it would be a total headache to  keep up with that throughout filming so  she ditched them tossing the lenses in  the trash after just one night of  filming number 11. again stuff in the  eyes not fun mackenzie crook faced a  struggle with his contacts as well  instead of lenses to change his eye  color though the actor wore double  contacts to give the appearance of a  wooden eye when asked to describe the  feeling the first word he used was  uncomfortable it may not have been ideal  conditions but it definitely lent itself  well to his pirate acting  number 12. what kind of injury wasn't  there during production this one didn't  happen on set specifically but the  accident did impact the making of dead  men tell no tales johnny depp suffered a  brutal hand injury offset that led him  to being flown to the states to get a  surgery done just one month into the  process and this injury delayed filming  as they were just getting into the swing  of things and unfortunately for that  production it was just the first of a  few injuries that caused delay these  pirates all lived to tell the tale but  it was not easy and many of them didn't  leave unharmed somehow which scene would  you have been most nervous to tackle  [Music]
 

